Ladybird runs document_start scripts when the document element is
inserted, document_end right after DOMContentLoaded, and
document_idle at min(DOMContentLoaded + 200 ms, load completion),
each once per document with a catch-up for points a document reached
before it was fully active. Blink’s ScriptInjectionManager::RFOHelper
hooks DidCreateDocumentElement() for kDocumentStart and
DidDispatchDOMContentLoadedEvent() for kDocumentEnd, and arms
kDocumentIdle as min(DOMContentLoaded + kScriptIdleTimeoutInMs, load)
(script_injection_manager.cc); UserScript::MatchesURL() applies
exclude patterns and globs first, then matches, and
MatchesDocument() handles match_about_blank by the creator’s URL.
WebKit injects DocumentStart from HTMLConstructionSite::
insertHTMLHtmlStartTagBeforeHTML() and DocumentEnd from FrameLoader::
finishedParsing(), folds DocumentIdle into DocumentEnd, and matches
at injection time with UserContentURLPattern::matchesPatterns(url,
allowlist, blocklist), with UserContentMatchParentFrame for about:
blank (LocalFrame::injectUserScriptImmediately()). Gecko’s
ExtensionPolicyService::CheckDocument() runs on document-element-
inserted and Script.injectInto() awaits promiseDocumentReady for
document_end and Promise.race([promiseDocumentIdle,
promiseDocumentLoaded]) for document_idle; MozDocumentMatcher::
Matches() checks all_frames and match_about_blank first. Content
script CSS joins the document’s user sheet as WebKit’s
UserStyleSheet with UserStyleLevel::User and Blink’s
InjectStylesheet() into the user sheet collection do.

Each content-script CSS file is an author sheet of its own, with
its own URL as its base, ahead of the page’s sheets. Blink does
the same: UserScriptInjector::GetCssOrigin() returns kAuthor, and
StyleSheetCollection::PrepareUpdateActiveStyleSheets() puts injected
author sheets before the page’s. Gecko preloads each file URI in its
CSSCache and adds it as an AUTHOR_SHEET through windowUtils.addSheet(),
and WebKit’s WebExtensionContext::addInjectedContent() makes a
UserStyleSheet for each file, at UserStyleLevel::Author and with the
file’s own extension URL as its base.

When match_about_blank is set, Ladybird matches an about:blank or
about:srcdoc document by the URL of its nearest same-origin parent
or opener, as Blink’s ContentScriptInjectionUrlGetter::Get() does;
Gecko’s MozDocumentMatcher::Matches() uses the principal’s URL,
and WebKit’s LocalFrame::injectUserScript() the parent document’s.
None of them ever uses a base URL.
